CJK font (IMPORTANT)
--------------------
`tools/gen_font.py` subsets a font **from your own machine**. It auto-detects a
CJK font (Windows: SimHei/Microsoft YaHei; macOS: PingFang; Linux: Noto Sans CJK
/ Source Han Sans / WenQuanYi), or you can point it anywhere with
`--font PATH` / the `RW1_FONT` environment variable
(`python tools/gen_font.py --list-fonts` shows the candidates it looks for).

Those system fonts are proprietary, so the generated `device/main/rw1_font.c`
is GIT-IGNORED and must NOT be published as part of a firmware release.

For commercial/redistributable use, point `--font` at an open-license font
instead, e.g. Source Han Sans SC / Noto Sans SC (SIL OFL 1.1) or
WenQuanYi (GPL+font-exception), and re-run the script. The firmware only
requires the generated file to be present at build time.
